<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Étienne Regnault</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Étienne Regnault was the first commandant of Île <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a>, now Réunion, sent by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-east-india-company">French East India Company</a> in 1665 with a small group of colonists. Their settlement at Saint-Paul began the island's permanent population, later joined by survivors from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taolagnaro">Fort-Dauphin</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>. He governed the colony until 1671, laying the foundation of what became a French plantation island.</p></div>
